title: March 2024

@p2050_greens_absorption_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — a fixed March follow-up dissolves Zieloni, guarantees Poland 2050 the first three MPs, splits larger delegations with Nowoczesna and raises Hołownia's retained leadership ceiling without giving Lewica authority over the decision.
title: Zieloni dissolve into Hołownia's movement
subtitle: Poland 2050 gains the core Green delegation while any larger caucus splits with Nowoczesna
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 27
order: 9
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 3 and formation_coalition_code = "ko_psl_left" and p2050_comeback_stage = 1 and p2050_greens_absorbed = 0
on-arrival: {!
const greens = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record && record.id == "greens";
});
const p2050 = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record && record.id == "p2050_party";
});
const nowoczesna = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record && record.id == "nowoczesna";
});
const greenMandates = Math.min(
    Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0)),
    Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(
            Number(greens && greens.exclusive_seats) ||
            Number(greens && greens.mp_count) || 0
        )
    )
);
const p2050Transfer = greenMandates <= 3
    ? greenMandates
    : Math.max(3, Math.ceil(greenMandates / 2));
const nowoczesnaTransfer = greenMandates - p2050Transfer;
Q.p2050_greens_absorbed = 1;
Q.p2050_greens_transferred_mps = p2050Transfer;
Q.greens_nowoczesna_transferred_mps = nowoczesnaTransfer;
Q.p2050_comeback_stage = 2;
Q.p2050_comeback_status =
    "Independent Poland 2050 strengthened by the dissolved Greens";
Q.ko_seats = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) - p2050Transfer);
Q.p2050_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) + p2050Transfer;
if (
    Q.government_party == "ko" && Q.government_has_confidence &&
    !Q.caretaker_government
) {
    Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - p2050Transfer
    );
    Q.coalition_seats = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.coalition_seats) || 0) - p2050Transfer
    );
}
Q.p2050_holownia_retention_ceiling = Math.min(
    900,
    Math.max(
        720,
        (Number(Q.p2050_holownia_retention_ceiling) || 0) + 200
    )
);
Q.p2050_holownia_presidential_bonus = Math.max(
    13,
    (Number(Q.p2050_holownia_presidential_bonus) || 0) + 4
);
Q.p2050_incoming_bloc =
    "founder loyalists, institutional reformers and an absorbed green current";
Q.p2050_ideology =
    "Independent green institutionalism · anti-duopoly centrism";
Q.p2050_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.p2050_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.35;
Q.ko_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.ko_poll_momentum) || 0) - 0.35;
Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 6;
if (greens) {
    greens.active = 0;
    greens.allied = 0;
    greens.bloc = "p2050";
    greens.kind = "former party";
    greens.parent = "Polska 2050";
    greens.legal_status = "dissolved into Polska 2050";
    greens.list_committee = "p2050";
    greens.club = "p2050";
    greens.in_cabinet = 0;
    greens.independent = 0;
    greens.mp_count = 0;
    greens.sejm_mps = 0;
    greens.exclusive_seats = 0;
}
if (nowoczesna && nowoczesnaTransfer > 0) {
    nowoczesna.mp_count =
        Math.max(0, Number(nowoczesna.mp_count) || 0) + nowoczesnaTransfer;
    nowoczesna.sejm_mps =
        Math.max(0, Number(nowoczesna.sejm_mps) || 0) + nowoczesnaTransfer;
}
if (p2050) {
    p2050.active = 1;
    p2050.bloc = "p2050";
    p2050.leader = "Szymon Hołownia";
    p2050.parent = "Polska 2050";
    p2050.legal_status = "independent party with an internal green current";
    p2050.list_committee = "p2050";
    p2050.club = "p2050";
    p2050.mp_count = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0));
    p2050.sejm_mps = p2050.mp_count;
    p2050.organisation = Math.min(
        100,
        (Number(p2050.organisation) || 0) + 8
    );
    p2050.cohesion = Math.min(
        100,
        (Number(p2050.cohesion) || 0) + 5
    );
}
Q.news_headline = nowoczesnaTransfer > 0
    ? p2050Transfer + " Green MPs enter Poland 2050 and " +
        nowoczesnaTransfer + " join Nowoczesna"
    : p2050Transfer +
        " Green MPs enter Poland 2050 as Zieloni dissolves";
!}

= March 2024 — Independence acquires an organisation

Zieloni's board concludes that KO offers cabinet proximity without enough
autonomy, while Hołownia now offers an independent home with a national
platform. The party votes to dissolve. Its organisers and **[+
p2050_greens_transferred_mps +] MPs** enter Poland 2050 as a protected green
current rather than creating another electoral family.[? if
greens_nowoczesna_transferred_mps > 0: The remaining **[+
greens_nowoczesna_transferred_mps +] MPs** join Nowoczesna and remain inside
KO. Above three mandates, the delegation divides as evenly as possible while
Poland 2050 keeps at least three.?]

The transfer is literal in the Sejm ledger: KO loses only the mandates that
cross to Poland 2050; MPs joining Nowoczesna remain within KO's total. Zieloni
is deactivated as a party in every later party, committee and polling display.
Every former Green MP now counts under one of the two successor parties.

Hołownia has turned exclusion into a second founding, polling movement and an
organisational gain. Delegates who might once have treated him as a temporary
campaign brand can now see a party surviving outside PiS and KO. His chance of
keeping the leadership after the presidential cycle rises again.

- @p2050_greens_channel
- @p2050_greens_compete

@p2050_greens_channel
title: Recognise the transfer and open a climate-policy channel
subtitle: Work with the new current while accepting that KO regards the move as a raid.
on-arrival: p2050_relation += 5; ko_relation -= 2; climate_state_capacity += 3; institutional_trust += 1; news_headline = "Lewica recognises Poland 2050's new green current"

Lewica speaks to the current through Poland 2050 rather than pretending the
dissolved Zieloni organisation still exists. Joint work remains possible on
energy, transport and local adaptation; ownership of the MPs is not disputed.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the climate channel

@p2050_greens_compete
title: Contest the green vote without contesting the transfer
subtitle: Accept the parliamentary ledger and argue that ecological politics still needs a left economic programme.
on-arrival: p2050_relation -= 4; progressive_credibility += 3; climate_state_capacity += 1; urban_progressive_support += 2; news_headline = "Lewica accepts the Green transfer and contests its programme"

Lewica acknowledges that the MPs now belong to Poland 2050 and campaigns
against their programme rather than their legal status. The disagreement moves
to public investment, workers and the cost of transition.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the absorption to the events desk

@konkrety_hundred_days_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — the hundredth day is counted from live state rather than asserted, KO's deflection is aimed at a target the player's own December-to-February record selected, and every response changes what the local-election campaign three weeks later is about.
title: The hundredth day
subtitle: The audits publish, the Prime Minister explains, and the coalition finds out who the explanation is about
face-image: img/poland/events/donald-tusk-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 26
order: 6
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 3 and government_party = "ko" and caretaker_government = 0 and konkrety_stage = 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_stage = 4;
const num = function(value, fallback) {
    const parsed = Number(value);
    return Number.isFinite(parsed) ? parsed : fallback;
};
// The audited count is built from what this timeline actually did, not from
// the historical six. Every term below corresponds to a konkret that the
// player's earlier decisions either closed or left open.
let delivered = 4;
if (num(Q.kpo_bill_quality, 0) >= 2) delivered += 2;
if (Q.public_media_transition != "PiS-controlled public broadcasting") {
    delivered += 1;
}
if (Q.konkrety_scoreboard) delivered += 1;
if (num(Q.konkrety_ownership, 0) >= 60) delivered += 1;
delivered += Math.min(3, num(Q.konkrety_left_items, 0));
if (Q.konkrety_kwota_wolna == "Staged ladder agreed with PSL") delivered += 1;
if (Q.konkrety_kwota_wolna == "Traded for progressive financing") delivered += 1;
if (num(Q.abortion_delay_months, 0) > 0) delivered -= 1;
if (num(Q.government_coalition_dissent, 0) >= 45) delivered -= 1;
Q.konkrety_delivered = Math.max(3, Math.min(18, delivered));
// Lewica is the junior partner: it can never claim more than half of a
// programme somebody else wrote, however good its paperwork was.
Q.konkrety_left_credit = Math.max(0, Math.min(
    Math.ceil(Q.konkrety_delivered / 3),
    num(Q.konkrety_left_credit, 0) +
        (Q.konkrety_receipts ? Math.min(3, num(Q.konkrety_left_items, 0)) : 0)
));
// Who the Chancellery aims at on the day is decided by the record, in order of
// how easy each target is to make stick.
if (Q.konkrety_scoreboard) {
    Q.konkrety_blame = "The published table";
} else if (num(Q.konkrety_ownership, 0) >= 60) {
    Q.konkrety_blame = "The whole coalition, us included";
} else if (
    Q.konkrety_line == "Publicly refused the list" ||
    Q.konkrety_kwota_wolna == "Killed openly by the Left"
) {
    Q.konkrety_blame = "Lewica";
} else if (
    Q.konkrety_kwota_wolna == "Left refused to carry KO's retreat" ||
    num(Q.psl_relation, 45) < 35
) {
    Q.konkrety_blame = "Third Way";
} else {
    Q.konkrety_blame = "The partners, unnamed";
}
Q.government_delivery += Q.konkrety_delivered >= 10 ? 3 : -3;
Q.public_trust += Q.konkrety_delivered >= 10 ? 1 : -3;
Q.ko_poll_momentum += Q.konkrety_delivered >= 10 ? 0.1 : -0.25;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_salience += 6;
Q.news_headline =
    "Day one hundred: " + Q.konkrety_delivered + " of the hundred konkrety are complete";
!}

= 22 March 2024 — [+ konkrety_delivered +] of a hundred

The hundredth day of the government arrives with three separate audits and
three separate numbers, because the government counts konkrety that are *in
progress* and the fact-checkers do not. On the strict count, **[+
konkrety_delivered +]** of the hundred are finished.

The finished ones are real and mostly small. State funding for in-vitro
restored by the Prime Minister's first signature. Logging stopped in the most
valuable forest stands. The children's helpline funded again and the
children's rights commissioner replaced. A Ministry of Industry seated in
Katowice. And the European money, which is the largest single item on the list
and the one nobody in the Chancellery describes as anybody else's work.

[? if konkrety_delivered >= 10: It is more than the historical record would
have predicted, and it is still not a hundred. The gap between *[+
konkrety_delivered +]* and *a hundred* is the only arithmetic the evening
bulletins can do.?][? if konkrety_delivered < 10: PiS parliamentary leader
**Mariusz Błaszczak** supplies the line of the day — *there were supposed to be
a hundred konkrety for a hundred days; there are no konkrety, there are a
hundred frauds* — and it is repeated for a week because nothing better is
available to contradict it.?]

Health Minister **Izabela Leszczyna** gives the government's defence: the
ministries were found in a worse state than anyone admitted, the backlogs were
concealed, and a hundred days was never long enough. It is largely true. It is
also the fourth different explanation offered since January, which is how
explanations stop working.

Then Tusk takes the deflection out and uses it in front of cameras.

[? if konkrety_blame = "Lewica": He does not use the word *Lewica*. He does not
need to: he says that some promises could not be kept because a partner in this
coalition refused to carry them, and every correspondent in the room writes the
same name down, because we said it ourselves in December and again in
February.?]
[? if konkrety_blame = "Third Way": He notes that this government has to
legislate with partners who campaigned on a different programme, and that
several of the hundred cannot pass the Sejm as things stand. Paszyk's phone
starts ringing before the conference ends.?]
[? if konkrety_blame = "The partners, unnamed": He returns to the formula that
has served him since January — a coalition of four parties, a hostile
President, a veto that cannot be overridden — and names nobody at all, which
leaves three parties to be suspected equally.?]
[? if konkrety_blame = "The whole coalition, us included": He speaks in the
first person plural throughout, which is generous and expensive: *we* promised
a hundred and *we* have delivered [+ konkrety_delivered +]. Having adopted the
list in December, we are inside every sentence of that.?]
[? if konkrety_blame = "The published table": He cannot deflect, because the
delivery committee published the table on the twentieth and every journalist in
the room has the blocking column open on a laptop. He is asked, twice, to
explain a row with his own ministry's name in it.?]

[? if konkrety_left_credit > 0: Of the finished konkrety, **[+
konkrety_left_credit +]** carry our ministry, our bill or our signature, and we
can prove it.?][? if konkrety_left_credit = 0: Not one of the finished konkrety
has our name on it in a form we can show a camera.?]
[? if abortion_delay_months > 0: The abortion bills are not among them. They
have not been scheduled, which is the one omission this coalition was formed to
avoid.?]
[? if konkrety_kwota_wolna = "Killed openly by the Left": Konkret four — the
sixty-thousand allowance — is listed as not delivered, with our February
statement quoted underneath it.?]

Local elections are three weeks away.

- @days_counter
- @days_confront
- @days_replan
- @days_walkout
- @days_podium

@days_counter
title: Publish our own audit, line by line, on the same afternoon
subtitle: Requires the annex or the delivery table. Answers a narrative with a document while the cameras are still on the subject.
choose-if: konkrety_receipts = 1 or konkrety_scoreboard = 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no written record of who owned which konkret, so our version of the hundred days would be one more opinion on a day already full of them.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_audit_response = "Counter-audit";
Q.media_capacity += 5;
Q.public_trust += 4;
Q.institutional_trust += 4;
Q.parliament_visibility += 3;
Q.issue_ownership += 3;
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 5;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 4;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.2;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica publishes its own hundred-day audit with a name beside every row";
!}

We publish at four in the afternoon, while the Prime Minister's conference is
still being clipped. One page per konkret we ever claimed, one line per
konkret we never did, and for the whole hundred a column headed *responsible
ministry* filled in from the government's own documents.

[? if konkrety_left_credit > 0: [+ konkrety_left_credit +] rows are ours and
are green. That is a small number and it is a checkable one, which is more than
anybody else on this stage can offer today.?][? if konkrety_left_credit = 0:
None of the green rows are ours, and we say so on the first page rather than
letting somebody else find it on the third. What we can show is which rows were
never ours to begin with.?]

The document is boring, it is correct, and it ends the deflection inside
seventy-two hours — not because it wins an argument but because it makes the
argument expensive. A Chancellery that has to answer rows cannot go on
answering with atmosphere.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the counter-audit

@days_confront
title: Answer him from the chamber, by name, the same week
subtitle: Available only when the Prime Minister has aimed at us. Ends the pretence of a coalition that argues in private; the fight is now the story into the local elections.
choose-if: konkrety_blame = "Lewica"
unavailable-subtitle: The Prime Minister did not aim at us, and picking up an accusation nobody made would be the most expensive way to become its subject.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_audit_response = "Confrontation";
Q.konkrety_ownership = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.konkrety_ownership) || 0) - 20
);
Q.media_capacity += 6;
Q.parliament_visibility += 6;
Q.movement_autonomy += 5;
Q.progressive_credibility += 4;
Q.party_unity -= 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 10;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 9;
Q.psl_relation += 4;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.25;
Q.coalition_blur = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.coalition_blur) || 8) - 5);
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left answers the Prime Minister in the chamber and names the promises he assigned to it";
!}

Żukowska takes the floor and reads the list back. Which konkret, which
ministry, which meeting, which date. She reads out konkret four and the
forty-eight billion złoty that was never in any budget he presented. She reads
out the promises this coalition made to women in October and asks him to name
the partner that scheduled them.

The chamber is loud for eleven minutes. It is the most-watched parliamentary
exchange since the formation and it is a genuine rupture: two governing parties
have now called each other liars on the record, three weeks before an election
in which they need each other's transfers.

We have stopped being the party that gets blamed. We have become the party that
fights in public, which is worth more to our voters and less to the government
we are part of.

- @poland_event_queue: Answer in the chamber

@days_replan
title: Force a written re-plan: every remaining konkret gets an owner and a date
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Converts a bad day into a delivery mechanism; the term's remaining promises become checkable, including ours.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A hundred-item replan needs staff across every ministry and the party has none free.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.konkrety_audit_response = "Written re-plan";
Q.konkrety_scoreboard = 1;
Q.konkrety_receipts = 1;
Q.government_delivery += 5;
Q.institutional_trust += 5;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.negotiation_capital += 2;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.government_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 3
);
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The coalition re-plans the hundred konkrety with a named owner and a date for each";
!}

We treat the hundredth day as an administrative failure rather than a
rhetorical one, which is the least satisfying available response and the only
one that changes the next two years. Every unfinished konkret is assigned a
ministry, a legal instrument and a quarter. Anything that cannot pass this Sejm
is marked as such, in writing, with the party that blocks it named.

Fourteen items are marked *will not pass*. Tusk signs it anyway, because
refusing to sign a delivery plan on the day the delivery figures are published
is not a thing a prime minister can do.

Nobody covers this. In September, when the next audit runs, it will be the
reason the number is not embarrassing again — and it is also, permanently, a
document that can be used against us.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign the re-plan

@days_walkout
title: Leave the joint conference and campaign on our own items
subtitle: Trades the government's platform for a separate identity three weeks before the local elections; whatever the coalition delivers after this belongs visibly to somebody else.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_audit_response = "Separate campaign";
Q.konkrety_ownership = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.konkrety_ownership) || 0) - 25
);
Q.movement_autonomy += 7;
Q.progressive_credibility += 4;
Q.issue_ownership += 5;
Q.local_network += 3;
Q.turnout_readiness += 4;
Q.coalition_blur = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.coalition_blur) || 8) - 6);
Q.ko_relation -= 7;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 6;
Q.government_delivery -= 2;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.15;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left leaves the hundred-day conference to campaign on its own promises";
!}

We do not stand on the platform while somebody else's hundred are counted. Our
people go to the regions instead and run the three weeks on the things we can
name: wages, hospital queues, housing, and whichever of our own bills is
furthest along.

[? if konkrety_left_credit > 0: We have [+ konkrety_left_credit +] finished
items with our name on them and we say each one out loud in every county town
we reach.?][? if konkrety_left_credit = 0: We have no finished items of our own
to name, so the campaign is about what we are still fighting for, which is a
harder sell and an honest one.?]

The cost is immediate and structural. A governing party that campaigns as
though it were not governing loses the ability to claim anything the government
does for the rest of the term, and KO's regional organisations are told the
same afternoon that transfers are no longer automatic.

- @poland_event_queue: Go to the regions

@days_podium
title: Stand beside him and defend the government's own count
subtitle: The coalition's easiest day and the movement's longest memory; the government's number becomes our number.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konkrety_audit_response = "Defended the count";
Q.konkrety_ownership += 20;
Q.ko_relation += 9;
Q.government_delivery += 2;
Q.government_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 6
);
Q.coalition_blur += 6;
Q.movement_autonomy = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 47) - 7);
Q.progressive_credibility = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) - 4
);
Q.progressives_dissent += 5;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.15;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left defends the government's hundred-day count from the same platform";
!}

We stand where we are asked to stand and we use the government's number,
including the *in progress* column. The pictures are good: four parties, one
platform, a hundred days survived.

It is the correct thing to do for a coalition that has to pass a budget, and it
costs precisely what it looks like it costs. Every organiser who spent 2020 on
the street watches a Left leader defend a count of [+ konkrety_delivered +] out
of a hundred, on the day the abortion bills are still unscheduled.

There is no version of the next audit in which we are outside the number. We
have joined it.

- @poland_event_queue: Defend the count
